.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH "skillastic enroll" 1  "skillastic enroll " 
.SH NAME
skillastic enroll \- First\-time setup: discover local repos, install the daemon, and make sure it survives logout/reboot
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskillastic enroll\fR [\fB\-\-system\fR] [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-interval\fR] [\fB\-\-init\-missing\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-depth\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
First\-time setup: discover local repos, install the daemon, and make sure it survives logout/reboot
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-system\fR
Monitor every user\*(Aqs repos and autostart at boot instead of login. Requires root
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOTS>\fR
Directory to scan for repos (repeatable). Defaults to $HOME for user scope, or /home for system scope
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<INTERVAL>\fR [default: 300]
Poll interval for each enrolled daemon, in seconds
.TP
\fB\-\-init\-missing\fR
Also run `skillastic init` for discovered git repos that have no .skillastic workspace yet, so they can be enrolled too
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-depth\fR \fI<MAX_DEPTH>\fR [default: 6]
Max directory depth to scan below each root
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Report what would happen without installing or starting anything
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
